      <activity id="fbbef508-f884-57d5-91eb-59be25a00a4f" activityNameId="6ab489c5-f64d-587c-b9c9-cfa7a3dfe7c9" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, EI 30 fire insulation, 50mm, 120kg/m3, reinforced alumium foil</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, EI 30 fire insulation, 50mm, 120kg/m3, reinforced alumium foil
Disposal of a insulation for fire protection of ventilation duct, made of 120 kg/m3 rock wool, for fire class EI 30, insulation thickness 50 mm, total weight: 7.1 kg/m2. Including cover with a reinforced aluminium facing and stainless steel wire mesh. Reference value of inventory is m2 area of duct surface.;
UUID: 4e9dcc2a-b4c2-4dcf-a607-094a5438cea0
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4e9dcc2a-b4c2-4dcf-a607-094a5438cea0.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
